{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/Kuvvius/status/2098038921301311753","id":"2098038921301311753","text":"We ran GPT-6 Astra on HumanCLAW-Bench, using the same open-source harness and motion generator.\n\nIt is a big step over the previous best:\n\n- FindSR: 64.9% → 75.5% (+10.6) \n- NavSR: 42.4% → 57.1% (+14.7) \n- InteractSR: 16.8% → 46.6% (+29.8)\n\nThe gains compound: Find-to-Nav conversion rises from 65% to 76%, and Nav-to-Sit from 39% to 72%. Astra also solves 147/507 (29%) episodes missed by all nine previous models .\n\nThree things stood out.\n\n1/ Better embodied spatial awareness\n\nGPT-6 Astra's dDtb—how far the objects it disturbs end up moving—is 0.65 m, the lowest on the leaderboard, while its #Dtb, the number of objects it touches, remains in line with the other models. It still bumps into things; it just does not keep shoving them.\n\n2/ Stronger spatial memory\n\nSitting is the hard case: the agent has to turn away from the target, so the seat leaves its ego view and it must rely on its own history. Earlier models often sat on the wrong object or on thin air. GPT-6 Astra converts 72% of successful approaches into a correct sit, up from 39%. Once it reaches the target, it never forgets to sit (0 of 108 failures).\n\n3/ Better agentic decision continuity\n\nEarlier VLMs often jump between decisions: sit down, stand up again, then wander off. GPT-6 Astra commits. Among episodes where a sit lands on the target, 97% end still seated with a clean stop, compared with 78% for Gemini 3.1. It knows what it is doing and finishes it.\n\n⚠️ Caveats: this is a single run in the low-thinking setting, and 53% of sit episodes still fail. \n\nEmbodied self-awareness remains the bottleneck we described in the paper; the ceiling has simply moved up.\n\nLeaderboard: http://human-claw.github.io\nAll 1,218 episode videos: http://huggingface.co/datasets/Choiszt/humanclaw-gpt6-lowthinking-results-logs","raw_text":{"text":"We ran GPT-6 Astra on HumanCLAW-Bench, using the same open-source harness and motion generator.\n\nIt is a big step over the previous best:\n\n- FindSR: 64.9% → 75.5% (+10.6) \n- NavSR: 42.4% → 57.1% (+14.7) \n- InteractSR: 16.8% → 46.6% (+29.8)\n\nThe gains compound: Find-to-Nav conversion rises from 65% to 76%, and Nav-to-Sit from 39% to 72%. Astra also solves 147/507 (29%) episodes missed by all nine previous models .\n\nThree things stood out.\n\n1/ Better embodied spatial awareness\n\nGPT-6 Astra's dDtb—how far the objects it disturbs end up moving—is 0.65 m, the lowest on the leaderboard, while its #Dtb, the number of objects it touches, remains in line with the other models. It still bumps into things; it just does not keep shoving them.\n\n2/ Stronger spatial memory\n\nSitting is the hard case: the agent has to turn away from the target, so the seat leaves its ego view and it must rely on its own history. Earlier models often sat on the wrong object or on thin air. GPT-6 Astra converts 72% of successful approaches into a correct sit, up from 39%. Once it reaches the target, it never forgets to sit (0 of 108 failures).\n\n3/ Better agentic decision continuity\n\nEarlier VLMs often jump between decisions: sit down, stand up again, then wander off. GPT-6 Astra commits. Among episodes where a sit lands on the target, 97% end still seated with a clean stop, compared with 78% for Gemini 3.1. It knows what it is doing and finishes it.\n\n⚠️ Caveats: this is a single run in the low-thinking setting, and 53% of sit episodes still fail. \n\nEmbodied self-awareness remains the bottleneck we described in the paper; the ceiling has simply moved up.\n\nLeaderboard: https://t.co/DCeh5PG4Qb\nAll 1,218 episode videos: https://t.co/sIZFjanDFJ","display_text_range":[0,1733],"facets":[{"type":"bold","indices":[6,18]},{"type":"media","indices":[273,296],"id":"2098038779349192704","display":"pic.x.com/SqUQcGarwM","original":"https://t.co/SqUQcGarwM","replacement":"https://x.com/Kuvvius/status/2098038921301311753/video/1"},{"type":"media","indices":[273,296],"id":"2098038827546005504","display":"pic.x.com/SqUQcGarwM","original":"https://t.co/SqUQcGarwM","replacement":"https://x.com/Kuvvius/status/2098038921301311753/video/1"},{"type":"media","indices":[273,296],"id":"2098038852707565568","display":"pic.x.com/SqUQcGarwM","original":"https://t.co/SqUQcGarwM","replacement":"https://x.com/Kuvvius/status/2098038921301311753/video/1"},{"type":"bold","indices":[357,365]},{"type":"hashtag","indices":[598,602],"original":"Dtb"},{"type":"url","indices":[1660,1683],"original":"https://t.co/DCeh5PG4Qb","replacement":"http://human-claw.github.io","display":"human-claw.github.io"},{"type":"url","indices":[1710,1733],"original":"https://t.co/sIZFjanDFJ","replacement":"http://huggingface.co/datasets/Choiszt/humanclaw-gpt6-lowthinking-results-logs","display":"huggingface.co/datasets/Chois…"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"Kuvvius","url":"https://x.com/Kuvvius","id":"1635560727284191232","followers":609,"following":345,"likes":262,"media_count":78,"name":"Jiawei Gu","description":"","raw_description":{"text":"","facets":[]},"location":"","banner_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1635560727284191232/1762432134","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2046841522637922304/td5r5aEP_200x200.jpg","joined":"Tue Mar 14 08:37:49 +0000 2023","protected":false,"website":{"url":"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=7p8yEHAAAAAJ&hl=En","display_url":"scholar.google.com/citations?user…"},"verification":{"verified":true,"verified_at":null,"type":"individual"},"avatar_color":null},"replies":3,"retweets":7,"likes":63,"bookmarks":30,"quotes":4,"created_at":"Thu Sep 10 13:20:33 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1789046433,"possibly_sensitive":false,"views":13629,"is_note_tweet":true,"community_note":null,"lang":"en","replying_to":null,"replying_to_status":null,"media":{"all":[{"id":"2098038779349192704","url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2098038779349192704/vid/avc1/932x1052/C